A||N||4||FIERO1985||EGR Problems PLease HELP!!!||||1||
Z||000000||FIERO1985||03-27-2001||09:46 PM||||<BR>Ok, heres the deal my idle has been erratic lately it will usually die at idle when hot or just act wierd at idle(jump up and down) I then got an EGR code. I replaced the valve after doing a vacume test and replaced it. But now I have the code again?? How do I know if it is the Selinoid or the tube? What are your suggestions??<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-27-2001||09:49 PM||||Well I can assume this is a V6 since you mentioned something about a tube.  The EGR tube cracks quite a bit with the V6's.  You can easily see if part of the cause of your troubles is the tube by feeling under it and seeing if it is broken anywhere.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Homer||03-27-2001||10:27 PM||||See my post 2 down from yours on the same subject.... It will most likely be that the EGR tube is busted under the upper plenum. What code is it giving you? #32?<P>If that's not it then check your IAC "Idle Air Control" also check your O2 sensor and the TPS "throttle possition sensor" all of these will shoot code #32 or #35 at ya...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rocketmad_1.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/homer_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||shain||03-28-2001||04:52 AM||||as for the erratic idle RPM, check your ignition coil. <BR>also it may be due to a crack/leak in your in your EGR valve.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jerpro||03-28-2001||08:22 AM||||this is a fast test you can doo to yur car.<BR>When cold, turn the car oon *engine running*<BR>and depress the gas pedal to about 4000 rpm and let it go immediately. If the rpm's go down unevenly and the car stalls when it gets back to 500 rpm or dies on you. It is the IAC. Simply get carb cleaner and spray the iac clean. Carefull with torqeing it too much. Stick with manufacturers specs.<BR> ||||reg||1
